; Return the machine to its home corner.
; Z lifts fully first (machine Z0 is the top of travel), then X/Y move.
; G53 = machine coordinates, so work offsets (G54 etc.) are ignored.
;
; Called by the PARK user button, and appended to the end of every job by
; custom_filter.py.
;
; G1 F1150, not G0: a rapid runs at each joint's own MAX_VELOCITY (3000 mm/min
; on Y and Z), which is faster than this machine is wanted to park at. A feed
; move holds the whole park to the same 1150 mm/min as the jog rate. The feed
; override slider still scales it, as it does any G1.
o<park> sub

  #<park_feed> = 1150
  #<entry_feed> = #<_feed>

  G53 G1 Z0 F#<park_feed>
  G53 G1 X0 Y0 F#<park_feed>

  ; Leave the modal state as it was found, so a job that parks mid-stream is
  ; not left in G1 at the park feed. F0 is an error, so only restore a feed
  ; that was actually set.
  o<restore> if [#<entry_feed> GT 0]
    F#<entry_feed>
  o<restore> endif
  G0

o<park> endsub
